> I have two magic markers, but I'm short on Enchant
> Weapon, so I was kind of saving them for writing
> those, when I've got my melee weapons sorted out[1].

Two magic markers, with recharging, should usually be
enough to significantly enchant at least one weapon and
still write a couple of scrolls of genocide, unless the
RNG is particularly mean to you.

If you want to insist on +7, and have to make multiple
retries at it (disenchanting back to +5 after getting +6
repeatedly), that could use up both markers, I suppose.

But if you're willing to settle for +6 (and can bless a
stack of blank scrolls before writing on them, holding
back at least one uncursed blank scroll in case you
get to +4), taking one weapon one scroll's worth past
+5 uses no more than six scrolls, usually fewer (five
is typical; three is the unlikely theoretical minimum),
at 16 ink (8-15 charges) each.  If you also had to
write the two scrolls of charging (at the same cost
as enchant weapon), a typical case would be you
use about eighty charges (plus or minus a few for
not-quite-average luck), but for a post-quest
Tourist make that about 60 charges (with the
same caveat), because blessed charging is free.

Magic markers from non-bones sources typically
come with 40+ charges each initially, and blessed
charging will usually bring them to 50 (provided
they haven't already been recharged, of course).

(If the markers are from bones and you haven't
formally identified them, all bets are off.)

