Magicbane is a reasonably good weapon for a Tourist,
and has the advantage of providing magic resistance.
(The platinum card does that also, but it's your quest
artifact, which can be a problem in the late game due
to Rodney, according to the wiki.)  I'd keep Magicbane,
if it were me.  You might want to #twoweapon with a
silver saber, if you can get one, particularly in Gehennom.

Another option is Grayswandir, but for a Tourist that probably
requires artifact wishing, and you already have Magicbane
and the platinum card and two Brands makes at least four
artifacts, so you could easily run through multiple wishes
trying.  (This is also a significant argument against doing
a lot of sacrificing before the castle, especially for a neutral
non-wizard: even if you don't want to wish for a weapon,
your chances of getting the Eye of Casting Spells As Often
As You Please and Teleporting Whenever You Want are
greatly reduced.  The ability to usefully cast spells, even
though you don't have the weapon limitations of the major
spellcasting roles, is a key advantage to being a Tourist,
although the platinum card is an even bigger advantage.
Tourists have to get *something* in exchange for their
execrable starting stats.)


